        "kind": "pull_request",
        "title": "fix(session-memory): bound session transcript reads to prevent OOM",
        "body": "## What Problem This Solves\n\n`getRecentSessionContent` in `src/hooks/bundled/session-memory/transcript.ts` reads session transcript JSONL files with an unbounded `fs.promises.readFile` call. A runaway or corrupted session file could force the session-memory extraction path to buffer the entire file into memory, leading to OOM.\n\n## Why This Change Was Made\n\nSession-memory extraction now streams the transcript newest-first through the shared `streamSessionTranscriptLinesReverse` helper, collects up to the 16 MiB tail, and reverses the lines back into chronological order before running the existing sanitizer/provenance filter pipeline. This reuses the project's existing bounded reverse JSONL reader instead of adding a second tail scanner, and it avoids whole-file buffering.\n\n## User Impact\n\nSession-memory extraction now safely bounds oversized transcripts while still keeping the most recent messages available for context.\n\n## Evidence\n\n- Added a regression test that writes a transcript exceeding the 16 MiB cap with recent trailing messages and asserts those recent messages are preserved.\n- Local focused run: `node scripts/run-vitest.mjs src/hooks/bundled/session-memory/transcript.test.ts --run` passes (4/4 tests).\n\n## Real behavior proof (standalone)\n\nI ran a standalone Node script outside Vitest that imports the actual changed helper from source (`src/hooks/bundled/session-memory/transcript.ts`) and exercises a transcript larger than the 16 MiB cap where the trailing lines contain recent messages.\n\nScript: `/tmp/proof-101475.mjs` (not committed).\n\n```text\n$ node --import tsx /tmp/proof-101475.mjs\n=== Oversized transcript ===\nFile size: 17826089 bytes (cap is 16777216 bytes)\nResult contains recent user message: true\nResult contains recent assistant message: true\nResult does NOT contain the huge early message: true\n```\n\nThe helper streams only the tail of the oversized file through the shared reverse reader, skips the partial first line, and returns the recent messages without buffering the entire transcript into memory.\n",
        "branch": "fix/bound-session-memory-transcript-read",
        "head_sha": "1f514a8d9fd941fbd7e96537e5a967e53dac4936",
        "author": "cxbasdev",
